  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will be overhead this weekend. After morning fog\nburns off this morning, expect mostly sunny skies with highs in\nthe mid to upper 70s. Overnight will be clear and cool again,\nwith lows into the low 50s. \n\nHigh pressure slides east on Sunday and warm and humid \nsouthwest return flow takes hold. Temperatures will rise into \nthe low 80s and dewpoint values into the mid 60s. Models have \nsped up a midlevel impulse for Sunday afternoon/evening. Shower \nand thunderstorm chances will be more likely now earlier in the\nday Sunday, vs. previous model progs that were showing the wave\npushing through Sunday night into Monday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nThere is potential for showers and thunderstorms several days \nnext week. A large upper level ridge sets up over the Eastern \nCONUS. Our area will likely be on the outer periphery of this \nridge with fairly strong westerly flow aloft. Several shortwave \nimpulses are forecast to traverse the outer ridge throughout \nthe week, and this will create the potential for ridge rider \nthunderstorm complexes. Still too early to tell at this time, \nbut if the timing of one of the shortwave impulses aligns with \npeak daytime heating, then severe thunderstorms will be \nlikely, especially with the strong west to northwest flow aloft.\nAt this time, the latest model guidance shows some potential \nfor this on Wednesday afternoon, but again, it is way too early\nto forecast severe thunderstorm potential this far out, but this\nwill be something to watch over the coming days due to the\nfavorable pattern.",
